  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> carrying a current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is placed parallel to a long wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> carries a current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. The distance between two wires is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and currents flow in the same direction. The force acting on the wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> is :</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0089_e94b5a05388c.png\" style=\"width: 193px; height: 200px;\" />​​​​​​​</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> directed towards wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> directed away from wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> directed towards wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> directed towards wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>.",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>&nbsp;An attractive force will act normal to&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;towards <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> because the direction of the currents in the wires is the same.</p><p>Force exerted on length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> due to the magnetic field is given as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p>Given here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p><p>Putting the values, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>&nbsp;directed towards wire&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
